las-stark benchmark of record
  protocol              : 3 s discarded warm-up, then 5 timed repetitions,
                          mean +/- sample (n-1) SD, one machine, one process
  golden vector         : ../../evm/test/vectors
  measured ||z||inf     : 137885  (bound B = 137935)
  witness z             : 2816 coefficients

A. NormAir -- constraint (1) only: ||z||inf <= B
   trace   : 4096 rows x 39 columns (single segment)
   proof   : 52876 bytes
   warm-up : 27 discarded iterations
  phase                                mean (ms)    SD (ms)   (n = 5)
  prove TOTAL (trace+setup+prove)        110.821      0.212
  verify                                   0.470      0.020

B. RelationAir -- constraints (1) + (3) at d = 256, all n outputs, shared z
   trace   : 4096 rows x 135 main + 15 aux columns
   public  : 11008 field elements (A', t, c, w')
   proof   : 98419 bytes
   warm-up : 7 discarded iterations
  phase                                mean (ms)    SD (ms)   (n = 5)
  prove TOTAL (the like-for-like span)     442.157      4.501
    .. quotient witness build              1.993      0.030
    .. main trace build                    1.306      0.041
    .. prover construction                 0.007      0.002
    .. Winterfell prove()                438.851      4.505
  verify                                   1.319      0.042

C. Cost of proving (1)+(3) rather than (1) alone  [same protocol, same process]
   prove TOTAL : 3.99x   (110.8 ms -> 442.2 ms)
   verify      : 2.81x   (0.47 ms -> 1.32 ms)
   proof size  : 1.86x   (52876 B -> 98419 B)

SCOPE: this proves the ARITHMETIC of base_verify only. Constraints (2)
  SampleInBall and (4) the SHAKE256 challenge are NOT in the AIR: c and w'
  are public inputs, so z is bound to (A', t, c, w') and NOT to (c_tilde, M).
  'Winterfell prove()' is the whole prover -- trace low-degree extension,
  Merkle commitments, constraint evaluation, DEEP composition AND FRI --
  not FRI alone. No gas figure is claimed: none has been measured.
